{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandatory data collection on deaths linked to \u2018chemsex\u2019",
        "additional_details": "In our view, if we don\u2019t count chemsex-related deaths, we can\u2019t understand the scale of the problem. If we can\u2019t understand it, we can\u2019t prevent more lives being lost.\r\n\r\nEvery life matters. Every death tells a story. But right now, the UK does not record when a drug-related death happens in the context of chemsex.\r\n\r\nThis petition calls for better recognition through better data collection, and as a result better support \u2014 not to judge people, but to save lives.",
        "background": "Require the UK Government to introduce national recording of chemsex-related deaths and publish annual data to improve prevention, support and harm reduction",
